      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 3,
          "section": "3.1. Effects of sintering temperature on WHAs densification",
          "quote": "numerous H2O, O2, and N2 gas molecules are absorbed in the surface of powders during the HEBM process and in the storage term of powders. In the subsequent sintering process, these gases are dissolved in the W particles and exhausted with difficulty. Meanwhile, filling the liquid phase becomes difficult. These lead to the closed microporosity, which causes a decline in the relative density of the WHAs.",
